  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "World exploring right now has some flaws--having to find worlds to explore requires someone to have an idea of where they want to go, and has to then scroll through many worlds to decide on one to go through. Then, if you're traveling with friends, you have to set a portal with permissions and by that point, maybe some people have changed their minds.\n\nSo what if we had a configurable \"generate random portal\" button in the initial menu when you press the menu button? One that would generate a portal to a world within certain tags (that you set ahead of time) at a certain permission level? Of course, the worlds would have to be approved for general use ahead of time to be considered by the system.\n\nThis could take advantage of the tags that people put on their worlds and also provide a more immersive experience than scrolling through menus and typing all sorts of stuff in to get to a world that might not be what you were looking for.",
